{
  "slug": "claude-library",
  "name": "Claude Library",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "23 reusable skills, 2 agents, and smart hooks for any project. Covers the full development cycle: architecture mapping,\nimplementation planning, code review, safe refactoring, security-aware editing, quality audits, and 5 interactive learning\nmodules with persistent memory. Hooks auto-lint Python files, block destructive git commands, protect sensitive files, and\nauto-suggest relevant skills based on your prompt.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **29 skills**, **2 agents** and **3 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (29): `api-development-api-impl` (Implement inference endpoints consistently), `architecture-arch` (Build a mental model before touching code), `code-diagnosis` (Find bugs, anti-patterns, and refactoring opportunities in existing code), `commit-ready` (Update docs, check for bugs, check test gaps, and commit), `learning-algo-practice` (Algorithm and coding interview prep for data scientists), `learning-code-review-eye` (Train your code review skills for data science), `learning-codebase-mastery` (Deep understanding through active learning), `learning-concept-recall` (Spaced repetition for data science and engineering concepts), and 21 more\n- **Agents** (2): `code-reviewer` (Expert code review specialist), `learning-coach` (Persistent learning coach for all learning skills)\n- **Hooks** (3): `UserPromptSubmit`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install claude-library@claude-community` from `tabers77/claude_experiments`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 29,
    "agent": 2,
    "hook": 3
  },
